[Dead Code - Second Instance of the Same Duplicate-Function Pattern] (noted by Claude): 2026-09-09

Incident: summarize.py had a second, unrelated dead duplicate of a function that's actually live in trial_loading.py -- same pattern as the "Dead Code - Orphaned Duplicate Functions" entry from 2026-09-08, found independently this time via CodeScene rather than by hand.

Context:
Running a CodeScene Code Health pass (prompted by the user asking "Aren't there some codescene analyses to do here?") flagged trial_loading.py's _passes_metadata_filters at cc=13 (Complex Method) and 7 arguments (Excess Arguments). Cross-checking summarize.py's own _passes_metadata_filters finding (also flagged, 7 arguments) revealed summarize.py's version was a *different*, already-decomposed implementation (four small _check_experiment_filter/_check_model_filters/_check_temperature_filter/_check_timestamp_filter helpers ANDed together) -- not the same source shared between files.

Error:
grep confirmed summarize.py's _passes_metadata_filters and its four helpers were never called from anywhere; only trial_loading.py's monolithic version (called from _parse_and_build_file_metadata) was live. Unlike the 2026-09-08 instance, the dead copy this time was the *better* implementation and the live copy was the messy one CodeScene had just flagged.

Root cause:
Same root cause as the earlier instance: a refactor (unclear which one) produced a clean decomposition in summarize.py that was never wired up to replace trial_loading.py's original inline version, and never deleted either.

Resolution:
Verified the two implementations were logically equivalent (each of the four checks against the monolith's four conditions) before swapping. Moved the four helpers plus the clean _passes_metadata_filters into trial_loading.py, replacing the monolith; deleted the dead cluster and the now-unused matches_model_pattern import from summarize.py. Verified byte-identical output for the default run, and separately verified each filter dimension (--model, --temperature, --exclude-model, --experiment, --timestamp) still filters correctly, since this replaced a live implementation rather than deleting only-dead code.

Impact: trial_loading.py's Complex Method finding (cc=13) is gone; Code Health 9.33 -> 9.68.

Lesson: When two files define a same-named private function, don't assume the newer-looking or better-factored one is the live one -- check call sites in both directions. This is the second time this exact "orphaned decomposition, live monolith left in place" pattern has appeared in this codebase; worth a repo-wide grep for duplicate private-function names as a standing check after future refactors, not just when CodeScene happens to flag the live copy.

